 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding portion of an official roster of educational institutions in Saga Prefecture, followed by State Department documentation concerning the postwar Japanese textbook Primer of Democracy. The Saga roster details elementary schools, kindergartens, middle schools, girls' high schools, and specialized youth and vocational training schools, concluding with a reference map of Kyushu. The subsequent documents include a January 1949 despatch from the U.S. Political Adviser in Tokyo transmitting an English translation of Volume I of the Primer of Democracy, published by the Japanese Ministry of Education in October 1948. The textbook translation covers the fundamental philosophical principles of democracy, contrasting popular sovereignty and human rights with autocracy and totalitarianism, and surveys the historical development of constitutional democracy in England and the United States.",
